{"type":"text","timestamp":1790854409014,"sessionID":"ses_f08c2967effeRJDzMKrrYrxRRI","part":{"id":"prt_0f73da4fb001odbmbdwFTJNJIS","messageID":"msg_0f73d8748001Q0zABO9rnng7kZ","sessionID":"ses_f08c2967effeRJDzMKrrYrxRRI","type":"text","text":"The implementation is found. The bug is in `overlaps`: it uses `<=`, which makes touching intervals like `[1,2)` and `[2,3)` (sharing no integer point, since 2 is excluded from the first) and empty intervals like `[2,2)` report as overlapping. For half-open intervals the shared-point test must be strict: `max(starts) < min(ends)`.\n\n{\"action\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"intervals.py\",\"old\":\"    return max(left[0], right[0]) <= min(left[1], right[1])\",\"new\":\"    return max(left[0], right[0]) < min(left[1], right[1])\"}","time":{"start":1790854407419,"end":1790854409005}}}
